WEBVTT

00:03.069 --> 00:05.401
Here we are. Be it ever so humble.

00:05.572 --> 00:07.904
Wow, this is some house.

00:08.074 --> 00:10.804
If you ever decide to sell,
I want the listing.

00:10.977 --> 00:15.073
Well, you'd have
to kill my mom for it, so sure.

00:18.051 --> 00:20.019
- Can I make you a drink?
- Charlie...

00:20.186 --> 00:22.051
...we both know I'm gonna sleep
with you.

00:22.222 --> 00:24.315
You don't have to liquor me up.

00:24.991 --> 00:27.960
I've been doing this a long time.
Trust me, you'll want a drink.

00:30.897 --> 00:33.092
Oh, hey.
I didn't know you guys were home.

00:33.266 --> 00:35.962
- Lydia, this is my brother, Alan.
- Alan, hi.

00:36.136 --> 00:39.299
- Hi.
- So sorry to hear about your troubles.

00:39.472 --> 00:41.963
- Troubles? What troubles?
- Oh, maybe I have it wrong.

00:42.142 --> 00:45.976
Charlie, didn't you tell me he was divorced,
broke and living on your couch?

00:50.917 --> 00:53.545
I don't know what she's talking about.

00:54.487 --> 00:56.580
I am going through
a bit of a rough patch...

00:56.756 --> 00:59.816
...but I try not to think about it too much.
- Oh, good for you.

00:59.993 --> 01:01.790
I'd be suicidal.

01:03.229 --> 01:05.288
You hear that? You have options.

01:07.033 --> 01:09.968
- Anyway, this is my nephew, Jake.
- Hello, Jake.

01:10.136 --> 01:12.001
- Hi.
- So, what grade are you in?

01:12.172 --> 01:14.766
- Seventh.
- Well, don't you worry when other kids...

01:14.941 --> 01:18.308
...make fun of you.
You'll show them someday.

01:19.546 --> 01:22.606
- Nobody makes fun of me.
- You're kidding.

01:23.783 --> 01:25.546
Why would anyone make fun of me?

01:26.286 --> 01:29.551
And this is my housekeeper, Berta.
Berta, Lydia.

01:29.722 --> 01:32.850
Choose your words carefully, slim.

01:33.693 --> 01:36.059
Slim? Why, thank you.

01:36.229 --> 01:37.662
I watch what I eat.

01:38.298 --> 01:40.493
Going in or coming out?

01:47.640 --> 01:49.801
Hey, uh, why don't we forget the drinks?

01:49.976 --> 01:52.376
- Go out on the deck. Enjoy the sunset.
- All right.

01:52.545 --> 01:55.241
- Well, it was so nice to meet all of you.
- Uh-huh.

01:55.415 --> 01:56.848
Yeah.
- Sure.

01:58.785 --> 02:00.377
You didn't have to be so rude.

02:05.525 --> 02:08.050
You said they were laughing with me.

02:08.895 --> 02:11.420
Hey, I got my own problems.

02:39.092 --> 02:41.583
Oh, Charlie.

02:41.928 --> 02:44.123
No need to thank me.

02:45.298 --> 02:47.391
I wasrt going to.

02:49.135 --> 02:50.568
Excuse me?

02:50.737 --> 02:54.173
It was very nice. It's just if I'd known
you were gonna camp down there...

02:54.340 --> 02:57.707
...I would have given you a lantern
and some marshmallows.

02:59.579 --> 03:02.571
- Hey, I was just trying to be thorough.
- You were showing off.

03:02.749 --> 03:06.981
No, no, if I were showing off,
I'd have done it with no hands.

03:07.954 --> 03:11.048
So I can expect this kind
of effort every time we get in bed?

03:11.491 --> 03:14.460
Well, maybe not during flu season.

03:15.395 --> 03:17.625
And it's important to have variety.

03:17.797 --> 03:19.594
I'm not gonna swing for the long ball.

03:19.766 --> 03:21.597
Once in a while I'll lay down a bunt...

03:21.768 --> 03:24.999
And how did you manage
to turn this into a bad thing?

03:25.238 --> 03:27.103
It's not a bad thing.

03:27.273 --> 03:29.002
Thank you.

03:29.409 --> 03:32.810
Which is not to say if you were open
to suggestion it couldn't be better.

03:32.979 --> 03:35.345
Oh, really.
And how could it have been better?

03:35.515 --> 03:36.539
Ooh.

03:36.716 --> 03:40.846
- Looks like I pushed a button.
- Yeah, well, looks like I didn't.

03:41.187 --> 03:42.848
Charlie.

03:43.556 --> 03:46.218
You can push an elevator button
a hundred times...

03:46.392 --> 03:49.418
...it still won't come any faster.

03:51.631 --> 03:54.361
Fine. Maybe next time I'll take the stairs.

03:55.234 --> 03:59.728
Oh, come on. Don't be like that.

04:00.840 --> 04:03.172
You were magnificent.

04:04.077 --> 04:06.068
Astonishing.

04:06.646 --> 04:09.479
You've ruined me for other men.

04:10.616 --> 04:13.107
There, was that so hard?

04:14.020 --> 04:17.456
- You boys and your little egos.
- Okay, okay, stop.

04:17.623 --> 04:20.558
In this bed, we don't say "boys"
and we don't say "little. "

04:21.794 --> 04:23.591
Fine.

04:23.763 --> 04:27.722
- You want me to try again?
- No, I'm a bit chafed.

04:27.900 --> 04:30.425
Let's make the next few minutes
about pleasing you.

04:30.903 --> 04:33.064
A few minutes? That's all I get?

04:33.239 --> 04:36.766
Trust me, darling, with me
that's all you can handle.

04:43.816 --> 04:45.613
- Hey, Dad?
- Yeah?

04:45.785 --> 04:47.753
Do you like Uncle Charlie's
new girlfriend?

04:48.121 --> 04:51.022
Well, I just met her the one time, so...

04:51.190 --> 04:52.919
No, not really.

04:54.093 --> 04:55.651
You know who she reminds me of?

04:55.828 --> 04:59.559
The girls at school who think they rule
the world because they got their boobs.

05:01.334 --> 05:04.792
Well, I hate to tell you, buddy,
but they kind of do.

05:05.705 --> 05:08.765
I don't get it.
I wouldn't be mean if I had boobs.

05:09.308 --> 05:10.605
Well, that's very admirable.

05:23.456 --> 05:27.256
Hi there. I like you very much.

05:28.394 --> 05:30.021
Please don't do that.

05:30.396 --> 05:33.627
Do what? I'm just being nice.

05:34.167 --> 05:35.566
I'm serious. Cut it out.

05:37.703 --> 05:39.568
- Hey.
- Hey.

05:39.739 --> 05:42.401
Hello, big boy.

05:45.678 --> 05:47.976
You really need to get him into a sport.

05:49.582 --> 05:52.517
I'll need a sports bra.

05:53.252 --> 05:55.413
I said quit it.

05:57.123 --> 06:00.354
- What are you watching?
- I don't know, some Disney crap.

06:02.361 --> 06:03.828
Where's your girlfriend?

06:03.996 --> 06:06.396
Hey, my boob.

06:09.035 --> 06:12.869
- She had to go pick up her kids.
- Probably from therapy.

06:13.239 --> 06:16.106
- What's that supposed to mean?
- We don't like her.

06:16.442 --> 06:18.376
- Who's we?
- Me and Dad.

06:19.212 --> 06:24.673
No, no, I'd... That's not, uh...
I mean, she seems, uh, really...

06:24.851 --> 06:26.512
No, we don't like her.

06:28.020 --> 06:31.683
She might be a bit outspoken
but I happen to find that very attractive.

06:31.858 --> 06:35.123
She must be dynamite in the sack.

06:38.698 --> 06:42.361
- Where do you get this stuff from?
- Cinemax.

06:44.604 --> 06:47.232
Well, not that my sex life
is any of your business, but...

06:47.406 --> 06:50.034
It's not his business.
It's nobody's business.

06:50.910 --> 06:52.707
So, uh, what does she do for a living?

06:52.879 --> 06:56.440
Besides being a stone-cold beyotch.

06:58.918 --> 07:00.715
HBo.

07:04.590 --> 07:07.218
- She sells real estate.
- Oh, like Mom.

07:08.794 --> 07:10.989
No, not like Mom.

07:11.164 --> 07:16.158
Lydia sells high-end homes in Beverly Hills,
and Mom sells high-end homes...

07:16.335 --> 07:17.632
...mostly on the beach.

07:18.938 --> 07:21.406
- What are you getting so defensive about?
- I'm not.

07:21.574 --> 07:25.010
Lydia sells homes on the beyotch.

07:32.285 --> 07:34.651
All right, all right, that's it. Go to bed.

07:35.655 --> 07:38.749
I wasrt mean before I got my boobs.

07:46.232 --> 07:49.963
Boy, puberty is gonna hit him
like a shovel.

07:56.442 --> 07:58.637
- It's good to have you back.
- Thank you, Bobby.

07:58.811 --> 08:00.472
We haven't seen your mother here.

08:00.646 --> 08:02.341
Maybe you just didn't recognize her.

08:02.515 --> 08:04.813
Like Satan,
my mother can take many forms.

08:06.185 --> 08:09.052
- Good one.
- I'm ready to order.

08:09.355 --> 08:14.156
Of course. Apologies for the frivolity.
What would you like?

08:14.327 --> 08:16.727
- I'll have the seared ahi tuna fillet.
- Hmm. Good choice.

08:16.896 --> 08:18.523
- Very rare.
- That's how we serve it.

08:18.698 --> 08:20.256
Red in the middle, not pink.

08:20.433 --> 08:22.560
- Shall do.
- Lf it's pink, don't bring it.

08:22.735 --> 08:25.135
Give it to someone who
doesn't know what rare is.

08:25.304 --> 08:26.828
- Of course.
- Know what? Forget it.

08:27.006 --> 08:28.769
You won't get it right.

08:29.508 --> 08:32.204
- Is your salmon fresh?
- Flown in today.

08:32.378 --> 08:35.176
- What time?
- I'll ask the chef.

08:35.881 --> 08:38.315
Many forms. I thought you were joking.

08:40.319 --> 08:41.684
You eat here regularly?

08:42.455 --> 08:43.820
Not anymore.

08:44.690 --> 08:47.716
So listen, uh, about this weekend.
My ex is going to be out of town.

08:47.893 --> 08:50.418
- So I'll have the kids.
- Whoa, Lydia...

08:50.596 --> 08:54.430
...no one loves the little ones more
than old Uncle Charlie.

08:54.600 --> 08:57.433
Don't you think it might be
soon for me to meet your kids?

08:58.037 --> 08:59.527
I don't want you to meet them.

08:59.939 --> 09:02.999
- Why not?
- I'm careful about who I expose them to.

09:03.175 --> 09:04.938
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Please.

09:05.111 --> 09:07.773
Why can't I expose myself to your kids?

09:08.047 --> 09:10.345
I mean, why can't I meet your kids?

09:10.983 --> 09:14.851
- Please don't make me hurt your feelings.
- You can't hurt my feelings.

09:15.988 --> 09:18.923
All right, fine.
You're a professional boy toy.

09:19.091 --> 09:21.685
A perpetual adolescent leading
a dissolute life.

09:21.861 --> 09:26.355
You may have your uses, but you're not
the kind of man I want around my children.

09:27.099 --> 09:28.396
Oh.

09:28.567 --> 09:31.559
What made you think
that would hurt my feelings?

09:32.004 --> 09:35.531
Two o'clock. JetBlue from vancouver.
Would you like to find out the movie?

09:35.708 --> 09:38.233
Don't bother, I'll just have the capellini.

09:39.712 --> 09:42.647
And I'll have the pork chop
with a baked potato.

09:42.982 --> 09:45.542
How about a little angioplasty
for dessert?

09:45.718 --> 09:47.618
I like a nice pork chop once in a while.

09:47.787 --> 09:49.880
Fine, I'm not gonna tell you how to eat.

09:50.056 --> 09:53.219
Really? Even if I chew slowly
for your pleasure?

09:55.628 --> 09:58.722
Ahem. So yea or nay on the pork chop?

10:00.766 --> 10:04.099
I'll have the spinach
and goat cheese salad.

10:04.270 --> 10:05.567
- Good choice.
- Thank you.

10:05.738 --> 10:07.638
On the food.

10:13.846 --> 10:16.246
How many pieces of bacon
are you gonna eat?

10:16.415 --> 10:20.579
My record's 14.
I barfed but it still counts.

10:21.754 --> 10:24.746
Do you know what's gonna happen
if you continue to eat like this?

10:25.491 --> 10:27.721
Yeah, I'm gonna barf.

10:29.228 --> 10:32.629
Alan, doesn't this poor child already
have enough strikes against him?

10:32.798 --> 10:35.323
- He's fine, Mom.
- All right.

10:35.501 --> 10:38.368
When Jerry Springer
has to knock down a wall to get him out...

10:38.537 --> 10:40.767
...don't come crying to me.

10:41.273 --> 10:43.764
That wasrt Jerry, that was Dr. Phil.

10:44.443 --> 10:48.777
I'm not saying it wasrt a turn-on, I just
think you need to trim a fingernail. Oh.

10:48.948 --> 10:50.779
Hey, Mom.

10:51.917 --> 10:53.942
Uh, Mom, this is Lydia. Lydia, my mother.

10:54.153 --> 10:57.850
- Oh. Pleased to meet you.
- Likewise.

11:02.728 --> 11:05.196
Boy, I'm glad I stopped
coming to work high.

11:10.469 --> 11:12.562
So, Lydia, what do you do?

11:12.738 --> 11:15.138
I mean, besides my son.

11:17.576 --> 11:21.205
- I'm in real estate.
- How interesting. So am I.

11:21.380 --> 11:26.613
Oh, yes. Evelyn Harper.
I recognize you from your bus-bench ads.

11:26.786 --> 11:29.584
People all over town
are sitting on your face.

11:33.225 --> 11:35.420
Well, dear, maybe someday
if you work hard...

11:35.594 --> 11:38.495
...people will be sitting on your face too.

11:41.167 --> 11:43.067
Thank you. When I get to be your age...

11:43.235 --> 11:46.398
...I hope I won't be schlepping
to open houses to make a buck.

11:46.572 --> 11:51.339
Mm-hm. Don't say "schlep," darling.
You're a bit too vanilla to pull it off.

11:52.878 --> 11:56.211
So, Charlie, how long have you been seeing
this lovely woman?

11:56.849 --> 11:57.873
Uh...

11:58.050 --> 12:00.746
- How long has it been, sweetie?
- Are you telling me...

12:00.920 --> 12:03.445
...you don't remember when we met?
- The way he drinks?

12:03.622 --> 12:07.023
There's a good chance he doesn't remember
coming down the stairs.

12:07.426 --> 12:11.055
- Did his father drink?
- What choice did he have?

12:11.931 --> 12:14.422
- Charlie, don't be snide.
- And stand up straight.

12:17.736 --> 12:19.294
This is so weird.

12:20.039 --> 12:22.064
- Well, I really must run.
- Oh, me too.

12:22.241 --> 12:24.175
- Can I walk you out?
- Oh, how nice.

12:24.343 --> 12:27.972
Are you sure you don't want to stay
and finish putting on your makeup?

12:28.747 --> 12:31.477
That's okay, I'm done.
Would you like to borrow some?

12:31.650 --> 12:33.948
No, thanks.
I'm allergic to the drugstore brands.

12:46.265 --> 12:47.732
What?

12:48.033 --> 12:50.467
And they call you slow.

12:52.137 --> 12:54.765
- You're kidding, right? You don't see it?
- See what?

12:54.940 --> 12:57.170
- Lydia and Mom?
- What about them?

12:57.343 --> 13:00.835
Come on, Charlie. The only difference
between those two broads...

13:01.013 --> 13:03.345
...is you came out of one and...
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

13:03.516 --> 13:05.746
Hold it. Hold it.

13:11.557 --> 13:15.960
- You think Lydia's like Mom?
- No. We think Lydia is Mom.

13:17.062 --> 13:20.031
Okay. Okay, you guys are nuts.

13:20.199 --> 13:22.599
This conversation is over.

13:25.037 --> 13:27.028
Who calls me slow?

13:32.444 --> 13:36.574
I'll tell you. There's a lot of women
in this town who work in real estate.

13:36.749 --> 13:38.478
I thought this conversation was over.

13:38.651 --> 13:41.711
They all wear the suits and
the designer bags. It's like a uniform.

13:41.887 --> 13:44.048
They could be firemen.

13:44.223 --> 13:48.455
And Mom's Lexus is a two-door
while Lydia's Lexus is a four-door.

13:48.627 --> 13:51.494
- Worlds apart.
- It is worlds apart.

13:51.664 --> 13:55.464
The two-door is a selfish car.
The four-door is a family car.

13:55.634 --> 13:59.001
And you know why Lydia has a family car?
Because Lydia has children.

13:59.605 --> 14:01.539
Unlike our mother.

14:02.775 --> 14:03.969
Shut up.

14:04.677 --> 14:06.110
Charlie, it's okay.

14:06.278 --> 14:09.907
You've been working out your maternal
issues by having sex with other women.

14:10.082 --> 14:12.550
All you're doing now
is cutting out the middleman.

14:13.085 --> 14:15.019
Oh, that is just sick.

14:16.655 --> 14:19.317
My point exactly.

14:20.225 --> 14:22.625
Stupid idiot.

14:23.128 --> 14:25.119
He's just jealous.

14:25.297 --> 14:28.266
Lydia's smart and funny and sexy.

14:28.434 --> 14:30.800
Way sexier than Mom.

14:30.970 --> 14:32.528
Not that I think Mom is sexy.

14:32.705 --> 14:35.367
New thought, new thought,
new thought.

14:35.541 --> 14:39.705
Oh, Charlie, if you could get rid
of disturbing thoughts that easily...

14:39.878 --> 14:43.507
...I wouldn't be making a quilt
out of your old underwear.

14:44.783 --> 14:45.909
Hi, Rose.

14:46.352 --> 14:48.445
I brought you a little gift.

14:49.188 --> 14:50.678
&lt;i>Oedipus Rex?&lt;/i>

14:50.856 --> 14:54.189
It's about a guy who sleeps with his mother
and then pokes his eyes out.

14:54.360 --> 14:58.592
I'm giving away the ending because you
might be blind by the time you get to it.

14:59.098 --> 15:01.692
Where do you get this stuff?
You've never seen Lydia.

15:01.867 --> 15:04.734
No, you've never seen me see her.

15:05.204 --> 15:08.332
Lydia is nothing like my mother.
Why would I get involved...

15:08.507 --> 15:11.408
...with a woman who even resembles
the monster who bore me?

15:11.910 --> 15:15.437
Oh, are you gonna love this book.

15:17.816 --> 15:21.980
- Here. Mom wants to talk to you.
- Oh, great.

15:22.154 --> 15:23.553
Hi, Mom.

15:23.722 --> 15:26.748
Oh, Lydia. Very funny.

15:27.426 --> 15:30.259
- I thought so.
- I liked it.

15:31.463 --> 15:33.556
So, what's up?
You still coming over tomorrow?

15:34.700 --> 15:36.827
I thought your ex had the kids.

15:37.002 --> 15:40.096
Okay, well,
why don't you bring them over?

15:40.305 --> 15:43.604
Oh, please,
how could I possibly embarrass you?

15:44.343 --> 15:46.811
No, no, no.
I only do that when I'm drunk.

15:49.014 --> 15:52.381
Look, I swear I'll be on my best behavior.

15:52.551 --> 15:56.317
Great, I'll see you then, Mom...
of the year.

15:57.389 --> 16:00.017
Well, in my book you are.

16:01.493 --> 16:04.155
One word and everybody
gets their eyes poked out.

16:08.767 --> 16:10.826
Why do I have to play with kids
I don't know?

16:11.203 --> 16:15.537
Because Lydia's bringing them over
and I didn't have time to rent a clown.

16:16.875 --> 16:20.174
- Are they boys or girls?
- Beats me.

16:20.479 --> 16:22.879
- How old are they?
- Not a clue.

16:23.482 --> 16:25.109
Sounds like fun.

16:25.284 --> 16:28.048
Hey, they're kids, you're a kid,
how tough could it be?

16:28.320 --> 16:30.982
I mean, we're not breeding pandas here.

16:32.825 --> 16:36.192
All right. But if they're boys,
just don't call them little dudes, okay?

16:36.929 --> 16:39.193
- Why not?
- There was this guy Mom used to date.

16:39.364 --> 16:43.494
And every time he'd see me,
he'd call me "Little Dude. " He was an idiot.

16:45.003 --> 16:48.268
Okay. Okay, that's good stuff.
What else you got?

16:48.440 --> 16:52.206
No lame magic tricks, no head rubbing
and please, no high-fives.

16:52.377 --> 16:54.777
- Got it.
- And don't ask who wants ice cream.

16:54.947 --> 16:57.745
- Everybody wants ice cream.
- I understand.

16:57.916 --> 17:00.817
Even lactose-intolerant kids
want ice cream.

17:01.120 --> 17:03.748
- Makes sense.
- Whatever you do, don't try to pretend...

17:03.922 --> 17:07.221
...you're not sleeping with their mom.
We're not stupid.

17:07.626 --> 17:10.186
So if I do this stuff, her kids will like me?

17:10.529 --> 17:11.894
- No.
- Why not?

17:12.064 --> 17:13.656
You're doing their mom.

17:20.506 --> 17:23.839
Hello, Lydia. Hey, little dudes.
Give me five.

17:27.513 --> 17:30.505
All right. That's what I'm talking about.

17:31.016 --> 17:34.076
Don't worry, he's not the one I'm dating.

17:35.854 --> 17:38.049
- There they are. Welcome.
- Hello, Charlie.

17:38.223 --> 17:40.088
These are my sons, Andy and Joey.

17:40.259 --> 17:42.352
- Nice to meet you guys.
- Wrong.

17:46.265 --> 17:48.495
Shake hands with him, darlings.

17:48.700 --> 17:50.065
Hi.

17:50.302 --> 17:51.496
- Hey.
- Ugh. Not like that.

17:51.670 --> 17:53.433
- Shake hands like a man.
- I am.

17:54.706 --> 17:57.937
- Do you always have to embarrass me?
- Ha-ha-ha.

17:58.110 --> 18:01.375
What are you laughing at?
You're no prize either.

18:08.887 --> 18:10.320
Oh...

18:11.924 --> 18:13.482
What?

18:13.692 --> 18:15.125
Nothing.

18:15.727 --> 18:17.319
Excuse me.

18:43.555 --> 18:47.047
Hey, who wants ice cream?

18:53.899 --> 18:55.560
Sorbet, not ice cream.

18:55.734 --> 18:59.135
You don't want to turn into
a big tub of goo like your father.

18:59.872 --> 19:01.567
And those are expensive new shirts.

19:01.740 --> 19:04.971
If you stain them,
don't even bother coming back.

19:12.851 --> 19:16.014
- What now?
- Oh, nothing. Nothing.

19:16.188 --> 19:22.684
I was just thinking about mothers
and kids and crying.

19:24.162 --> 19:26.892
So much crying.

19:28.100 --> 19:31.695
- Well, what do you think of my boys?
- Oh, they're terrific.

19:31.870 --> 19:36.034
And the way you interact
with them is so unbelievable.

19:37.442 --> 19:41.742
Thank you. The older one has a chance.
The younger one I'm afraid is a lost cause.

19:43.715 --> 19:46.684
Anyway, we have the house
to ourselves.

19:46.852 --> 19:49.616
You feel like going upstairs?

19:49.788 --> 19:53.849
Uh... Yeah, that's a interesting idea.

19:54.026 --> 19:55.857
What's the matter, Charlie?

19:56.461 --> 19:58.361
It's kind of hard to explain.

19:59.031 --> 20:04.833
Well, why don't we go get naked
and see if that loosens your tongue?

20:07.239 --> 20:09.434
I got my nails done.

20:15.247 --> 20:18.182
Oh, why not? I'm going to hell anyway.
